{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbPmW6GdNcY47C4yXx8N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: CHANGES\n\n- P1 tests/budgets.rs:61 — `WATCH_BUDGET_MS = 6` and `MODELS_BUDGET_MS = 6` are 3x a 2ms reading. At that size, process-spawn jitter dominates. Slower Linux CI runners or a loaded macOS box will flake, and the issue says CI noise must not trip budgets. Fix: add a floor (for example `max(3x, 50ms)`) or use a fixed 50–100ms for those two, and say in the comment why the floor exists.\n- P2 tests/budgets.rs:64 — The criterion \"passes locally and on Linux CI\" is unverified. All measured values are from an M-series Mac, and the 8.7MB RSS budget has no Linux sample. Fix: run on Linux CI, record that sample, and set the budget from it.\n- P2 PR body — Acceptance criterion 3 (making `run` slow fails the test) and ruling 1 (record the negative control in the PR) have no evidence. The body has no sleep-injection run and no failing output. Fix: add the recorded negative-control result to the PR body.\n- P3 tests/budgets.rs:89 — `Env::new_info` copies `Env::new`, and the harness (`Env`, `until`, `FAKE_AGENT`) looks copied from `tests/cli_e2e.rs`. Fix: take the agent script as a parameter, or share a `tests/common` module.\n- P3 tests/budgets.rs:327 — The RSS test only waits for status RUNNING, not for the fake agent to have started, so \"while a fake agent runs\" is not guaranteed. Fix: wait for `agent.pid`, as the cancel test does.\n- P3 tests/budgets.rs:260 — The cancel test never checks that the grandchild `sleep 300` was killed. It can leak a process in CI. Fix: kill the `grandchild.pid` process in cleanup.\n\nSTATUS: DONE"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7056,"cache_read_input_tokens":29090,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7056},"output_tokens":5,